st rolling those  out um i have my xbox series x here  ta-da it is not plugged in  and i have intentionally had it not  plugged in  for uh 24 hours because i wanted to show  you guys something  so let me plug it in for you guys right  now i'm gonna try and do this video as  well without any editing so you guys can  fully see it all  okay here we go  okay it is plugged in pressing  controller on now let me make myself  smaller  controller i guess did not sync on that  one  but i'm turning the xbox on  okay here we go uh no startup like you  would normally have  from your xbox one x when it has not had  power is worth noting  um and then let's just  jump into ahri shall we  this is the point i am making other way  around it was on the other side  uh quick resume works even if the  console is off  to the extent that you can have the  console unplugged from power  for 24 hours this is my first time  attempting this um  or second actually i had moved it once  and realized that it worked that way  um i'm sure any other game that i've had  open recently  i think fable anniversary should also  quick regime um so basically the point  here is  again this thing was fully unplugged  from power and quick regime still  works uh the point of quick regime is  not  about you in a single play session in a  single five hour block of time  jumping between five games it is about  the people who only play  four games in an entire month having  them  thank you xbox 360 uh interface uh  having them on their home screen  and being able to jump through those  four games  um i would guess probably majority of  gamers play one or two games in a month  obviously i  imagine a lot of people watching this  video would probably be a little bit  more involved in the medium than that  i of course am but my point there is  quick regime works  always um even if the console is  unplugged from power even if it is moved  uh even if you've just turned it off  so that you can constantly access the  games that you are actively playing  significantly faster it's not about  jumping between  four games in one hour it's about  having them there quick resumable you  know if that's a word  uh for a month for a year for as long as  you want  those games are available to you you  don't have to watch the loadings any the  loading screens that that uh the startup  screens rather those aren't even loading  screens in a lot of cases they're just  startup um trailers basically or  advertising  uh for any of the games you frequently  play so that's kind of the point that i  feel like a lot of people have missed um  and i guess you could say like well that  feature's not that cool um you will  absolutely use it is the thing anyone  who plays more than one game will  absolutely use it and  and the feature is cool uh in a way that  i  feel is you know even if i i think it's  crazy that i can unplug this thing and  use it but  even if that doesn't seem like anything  to you i think what makes it cool is  that  quick regime can cut down jumping into a  game  by minutes when you add that up over a  month for the four games you're playing  in that month it can save you hours of  time uh  it is it is a massive time saver and it  is really convenient to have this  series of games that you really enjoy uh  really readily available on the day  where you feel like playing fable versus  the day where you feel like playing ahri  versus the day where you feel like  playing gears versus the day where you  feel like playing halo  so that that's kind of the point that i  wanted to make quick regime is not about  one session it is not about the the five  hour period like i keep saying that you  want to play  uh five games in it is about  always wanting to have these certain  games  available to you really quickly um so i  think it's really neat and really  impressive that it works even when it's  unplugged from power  which is you know the purpose of this  video really was to show you guys that  becau